3. MULTI-TENANT SAAS ARCHITECTURE
==================================================

UNEXA MUST NOT be designed as a single-college hard-coded application.

Architecture:

UNEXA PLATFORM
|
+-- College A
|   +-- Admin
|   +-- Co-Admin
|   +-- Moderators
|   +-- Students
|   +-- Departments
|   +-- Batches
|   +-- Years/Semesters
|   +-- Sections
|   +-- Classes
|   +-- Timetable
|   +-- Calendar
|   +-- Announcements
|   +-- Documents
|   +-- Branding
|   +-- Audit Logs
|
+-- College B
|
+-- College C
|
+-- etc.

Every college must have strict data isolation.

A student from College A MUST NEVER be able to access College B data.

An administrator from College A MUST NOT be able to modify College B data.

The platform Owner/SuperAdmin is the only role with global platform-level access.

Use a robust tenant-aware data model.

Every important document/data record should have a collegeId/tenant relationship.

Do not trust collegeId supplied by the client for privileged operations.

Validate tenant access server-side and through Firestore Security Rules.

