5. SECURITY REQUIREMENTS
==================================================

SECURITY IS CRITICAL.

Never trust Flutter/client-side UI for authorization.

A hidden button is NOT security.

A disabled button is NOT security.

A role stored only in local storage is NOT security.

A malicious user must NOT be able to modify Firestore data to become Admin.

A malicious user must NOT be able to modify their own:
- role
- collegeId
- approval status
- ban status
- permissions
- admin privileges

Use:

- Firebase Authentication
- Firestore Security Rules
- Cloud Functions
- Firebase Admin SDK where required
- server-side authorization
- tenant isolation
- custom claims where appropriate
- append-only audit logs
- server timestamps

Sensitive role/permission changes should be performed through trusted backend code / Cloud Functions rather than allowing arbitrary client writes.

Design secure Firestore rules.

Rules must verify:
- authenticated user
- college membership
- correct role
- correct permission
- target tenant
- ownership where applicable
- allowed state transitions

Prevent privilege escalation.

Prevent cross-college reads/writes.

Prevent students from modifying other users.

Prevent moderators from performing admin-only actions.

Prevent Co-Admins from performing Owner-only actions.

